<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>IRC channel logs</title><style>html {
  background: #fdfdfd;
}

h1 {
  font-weight: 300;
}

h2 {
  font-weight: 200;
}

h3 {
  padding: .5em 0;
  border-top: 3px dotted #ddd;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

form {
  width: 400px;
  display: flex;
}

input {
  width: 100%;
  display: flex;
  border-radius: .25em 0 0 .25em;
  border: 1px solid #aaa;
  border-right: 0;
  padding: 0.5em;
}

button {
  display: flex;
  border-radius: 0 .25em .25em 0;
  background-color: #007bff;
  border: 1px solid #007bff;
  padding: .5em;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: white;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: #0069d9;
  border-color: #0062cc;
}

a {
  color: #007bff;
  text-decoration: none;
}

a:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}

h4 {
  margin-bottom: .5em;
}

table td {
  padding: 0.75em;
}

table tr:hover {
  background: #eee;
}

.year {
  display: table;
}

.month {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-right: 1em;
}

ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.nick {
  padding-right: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: right;
  width: 13rem;
  display: table-cell;
}

.nick a {
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.message {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-left: 0.6rem;
  border-left: 2px solid #333;
}

.notice {
  color: #859900;
  font-style: italic;
}

.line {
  line-height: 1.8rem;
  display: table;
}

#logs {
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-09-13.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="015637"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#015637" label="[01:56:37]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">lrvick: give me or stikonas or Googulator a ping or open an issue on gh if you run into any issues with updating live-bootstrap ^-^</span></div><div class="line" id="080515"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#080515" label="[08:05:15]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Lance R. Vick&gt; Will do. I expect it to be a bit of a slog</span></div><div class="line" id="121119"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#121119" label="[12:11:19]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;cosinusoidally&gt; <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/cosinusoidally/tcc_bootstrap_alt/blob/dev/m2min/mk_awk_m2">https://github.com/cosinusoidally/tcc_bootstrap_alt/blob/dev/m2min/mk_awk_m2</a>  eliminated the use of a C preprocessor I can now bootstrap a heavily cut down C compiler using just awk (the same code can also be built under itself, or a C compiler, or a JS vm). mawk is also surprisingly small (128KB on my system, and it only depends on a libc).</span></div><div class="line" id="125244"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#125244" label="[12:52:44]">&lt;Googulator&gt;</a></span><span class="message">cosinusoidally: does this also work now using regular M2?</span></div><div class="line" id="131116"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#131116" label="[13:11:16]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;cosinusoidally&gt; my M2_simple_asm.c can be built by a regular M2, but M2_simple_asm.js cannot yet (this is the version that gets translated to awk). For M2_simple_asm.js I would need a trivial translation pass ( eg function foo(a,b,c) { ... becomes int foo(int a, int b, int c) { ...)</span></div><div class="line" id="131223"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#131223" label="[13:12:23]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;cosinusoidally&gt; I would need to create a &quot;js_to_c_simple.c&quot;</span></div><div class="line" id="131620"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#131620" label="[13:16:20]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;cosinusoidally&gt; I think I'm probably going to have a play around with creating awk versions of M0 and hex2 next.</span></div><div class="line" id="221920"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#221920" label="[22:19:20]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">cosinusoidally: glad to hear that you are enjoying your experiment.</span></div><br /></div></body></html>